@@ -63,6 +63,22 @@ fwctl --device sensor-0042 update sensor-node-1.2.0.fwpkg
 fwctl --device sensor-0042 status
 ```
 
+Field crews can split the update in two, because pushing an image over serial
+takes minutes while the window where a reboot is safe often lands hours later:
+
+```sh
+fwctl --device sensor-0042 stage sensor-node-1.2.0.fwpkg
+# the device keeps running its confirmed firmware until the reboot window opens
+fwctl --device sensor-0042 activate
+```
+
+`stage` transfers the image and verifies the device-side digest, then records
+what it staged in the staging journal. It never selects the candidate slot or
+reboots the device. `activate` finishes from that journal record alone: it
+reconnects, checks the device still matches what was staged, verifies the digest
+again, sets the candidate slot, reboots, health-checks, and confirms. The record
+is consumed either way, so a lost staged update has to be staged again.
+
 After an update, run `fwctl --device sensor-0042 history` to review the outcome
 recorded locally, or `fwctl doctor` if a device does not show up in `fwctl
 devices`.
